---
title: Mammals
description: Measurement fields for specimens in a Mammalogy catalog.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

Specimens in the `Mammalogy` catalog format show the mammal measurement form.
Weight units, sex, and life stage work the same way across taxon groups; see
[Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/).

## Measurements

- `Show outlier warnings`: on by default. Flags `Total length (mm)`,
  `Tail length (mm)`, `Hind foot length (mm)`, `Ear length (mm)`, and `Weight`
  values that fall outside the typical range for the same species (or genus)
  once the project has at least 10 comparison records. Turn it off to suppress
  warnings.
- `Total length (mm)`: length from the tip of the nose to the tip of the tail.
- `Tail length (mm)`: length of the tail from the base to the tip.
- `Head and body length (mm)`: auto-calculated as
  `Total length (mm) - Tail length (mm)`.
- `Tail/HB length`: auto-calculated as a percentage,
  `(Tail length / Head and body length) × 100`.
- `Hind foot length (mm)`: length of the hind foot from the base to the tip of
  the claw.
- `Ear length (mm)`: ear length.
- `Weight`: specimen weight in the selected unit.
- `Accuracy`: `Accurate` or `Inaccurate`. Choosing `Inaccurate` opens
  `Inaccurate measurements`, where you tick at least one affected measurement
  (total, tail, hind foot, ear, and weight, plus forearm and tibia when bat
  fields are shown) and can enter an `Accuracy remark`. Select
  `Select inaccurate measurements` to edit the selection later. Flagged fields
  are marked with `*` in the form and can be bracketed in exports and labels.
- `Sex`: select from the configured specimen-sex controlled vocabulary. Changing
  `Sex` prompts `Change sex?` and clears reproductive data that no longer
  applies.
- `Life stage`: select from the configured life-stage controlled vocabulary.
- `Remarks`: additional notes about measurements.

## Reproductive data

Male fields appear for `Male`, `Male?`, `Gynandromorph`, and `Hermaphrodite`.
Female fields appear for `Female`, `Female?`, `Gynandromorph`, and
`Hermaphrodite`.

| Sex | Field | Options / Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Male | `Testes` — `Position` | `Scrotal`, `Abdominal` |
| Male | `Length (mm)` and `Width (mm)` | Right testis; shown only when `Position` is `Scrotal` |
| Male | `Epididymis` | `Tubular`, `Partial`, `Not Tubular`; shown only when `Position` is `Scrotal` |
| Female | `Vagina opening` | `Imperforate`, `Perforate` |
| Female | `Pubic symphysis` | `Close`, `Small Open`, `Open`; shown when `Life stage` is `Adult` |
| Female | `Reproductive stage` | `Nulliparous`, `Primiparous`, `Multiparous` (`Adult` only) |
| Female | `Mammae counts (pairs)` | `Axillary`, `Abdominal`, and `Inguinal` pairs (`Adult` only) |
| Female | `Mammae condition` | `Small`, `Large`, `Lactating` (`Adult` only) |
| Female | `Embryo` | `Left` and `Right` counts, plus `CR length (mm)` (crown-rump length) (`Adult` only) |
| Female | `Placental scars` | `Left` and `Right` counts (`Adult` only) |

## Bat fields

Turn on `Show bat fields` on a specimen to add `Forearm Length (mm)`,
`Tibia Length (mm)`, and `Echolocate?`. Turning on `Echolocate?` adds
`Echolocation` (`FM`, `CF`, `QCF`, or `None`), `Frequency Max (kHz)`,
`Frequency Min (kHz)`, `Frequency At Max Energy (kHz)`, and
`Duration (seconds)`.

To show bat fields on every mammal specimen, turn on `Always show bat fields` in
`Settings` > `Catalogs` > `Format` (under `Measurement records` when `Mammalogy`
is selected). Once bat or echolocation data is saved on a specimen, the section
stays visible and cannot be toggled off.

## Parts and symbionts

Mammal catalogs include the `Symbionts` examination fields at the bottom of the
measurement form and the symbiont tab in `Specimen Parts`. See
[Symbionts](/en/usages/specimens/symbionts/).
